  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Papua New Guinea Growth and Resilience Development Policy Financing with a Catastrophe Deferred Drawdown Option</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed Development Policy Financing (DPF) aims to support the Government of Papua New Guinea in promoting fiscal sustainability, strengthening trade facilitation and market access, and enhancing resilience in the climate and health sectors. This is a standalone operation, designed around three Program Development Objectives (PDO) and Pillars to: (i) promote fiscal sustainability; (ii) strengthen trade facilitation and market access; and (iii) improve resilience to climate change, natural disasters, and health emergencies. This 150 million dollar operation consists of a 100 million dollar Development Policy Credit from the IDA Country Allocation and a 50 million dollar Catastrophe Deferred Drawdown Option (Cat DDO) (12.5 million dollars from IDA Country Allocation, 12.5 million dollars from the Crisis Response Window, and 25 million dollars from IDA general resources). The proposed operation aligns with PNG&apos;s national development plan and the World Bank&apos;s corporate goals. PNG&apos;s national development plan, the Medium-Term Development Plan IV 2023-2027 (MTDP IV), focuses on promoting broad-based economic growth, developing quality and sustainable infrastructure, and building educated, skilled, and healthy human capital. This DPO also supports reforms that address commitments in the National Prevention Strategy (2025-2030) to build peace and boost resilience and strengthen human development in PNG. The operation is aligned with the Corporate Scorecard, PNG Country Partnership Framework (CPF) FY2026-FY2031 and IDA21 priorities. The pillars and policy areas are selected based on their alignment with climate and disaster resilience priorities, their complementarities with other development partners programs, and the availability of technical assistance to support implementation. Given capacity constraints and fluid policy environment, the operation is designed as a single-standalone DPO, focusing on a compact set of front-loaded, high-impact reforms that are feasible within existing constraints.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To support the Government of Papua New Guinea reforms to: (i) promote fiscal sustainability; (ii) strengthen trade facilitation and market access; and (iii) improve resilience to climate change, natural disasters and health emergencies.</narrative>
